# The gating clang-tidy profile. It deliberately stays much narrower than the
# compiler lane and contains only checks that find reconstruction/type errors;
# style, naming and modernize checks are not applicable to decompiled source.
#
# Exclusions, with the binary/source evidence:
# - bugprone-narrowing-conversions / cppcoreguidelines-narrowing-conversions,
#   -Wconversion, -Wsign-conversion: VC6 source and the recovered corpus narrow
#   implicitly everywhere (GUI code int -> INT16), so as errors they demand
#   hundreds of suppressions without finding reconstruction errors.
# - bugprone-sizeof-expression pointer heuristics: recovered allocators
#   deliberately size pointer arrays (`sizeof(T*)`), which Clang reports as
#   "pointer to aggregate". The rest of the check stays on.
# - Imperialism-audit noise that mostly restated faithful compiler/source shape
#   or incomplete naming: bugprone-branch-clone, clang-analyzer-deadcode.DeadStores,
#   misc-redundant-expression, bugprone-assignment-in-if-condition,
#   bugprone-casting-through-void, readability-suspicious-call-argument,
#   bugprone-suspicious-memset-usage. Clang 19 already covers the useful
#   memory diagnostics in the compiler lane.
# - bugprone-virtual-near-miss: a trial only found srBinFStream::pseek/ptell
#   versus seek/tell, which are distinct virtuals. Remaining FunctionXXXXX
#   names would make its similarity heuristic worse, not better.
# - bugprone-multi-level-implicit-pointer-conversion: trial found implicit
#   T** -> void* at growable-vector / PList / FileRead / hash APIs. Those
#   opaque-storage boundaries should become explicit, but gating now would
#   demand a cast sweep rather than a reconstruction fix.
# - bugprone-copy-constructor-init: a hit means compare the constructor with
#   retail, not insert Base(other). Recovered copies such as stTextureAnim
#   and stLightDefinition deliberately reset registry/runtime bases.
# - bugprone-unhandled-self-assignment: hundreds of hits in vector/srArray/
#   srPtr assignment templates; too noisy to gate.
# - readability-duplicate-include: with HeaderFilterRegex it reports unique
#   #include lines as duplicates when a skipped system or sibling header already
#   pulled in the same spelling, and the same hits on self-contained headers
#   would delete required includes. Real same-file repeats stay a review item.
# - wiz8-redundant-scalar-cast, wiz8-bool-like-byte and
#   wiz8-project-record-reinterpret-cast are project-specific. Normal lint gates
#   only changed lines; WIZ8_REDUNDANT_CAST_LINES=* is the explicit full-corpus
#   audit mode for all three reconstruction-debt checks. Cross-record project
#   reinterpret casts have no source-comment waiver: reconcile the type/prototype.
#   Boolean-domain proofs include exact whole-record memset(..., 0/1, sizeof(T))
#   initialization. Predicate-shaped byte functions with missing bodies are
#   surfaced as non-gating warnings only when recovered code actually uses them.
#   A proven intentional byte boolean can use `bool-byte-ok: reason` on or
#   immediately above its declaration.
#
# The stock checks below the project-specific ones are gated because a
# whole-tree trial over all 295 recovered translation units found zero hits, so
# they add reconstruction-error detection without demanding a single
# suppression. They catch the failure modes a hand-recovered body actually
# produces: a botched comparison chain, a pointer-arithmetic operand misplaced
# into an allocation size, a malformed empty statement where a loop body
# belongs, a control-flow reconstruction whose loop can never terminate, and a
# reference member mistaken for an assignable pointer-like relationship. An
# empty `if (...) ;` or a genuinely infinite loop is never faithful source.
#
# bugprone-suspicious-string-compare is configured rather than left at its
# defaults: `if (strcmp(a, b))` and `!strcmp(a, b)` are entirely plausible
# period source, so only the actually suspicious result handling (`== 1` /
# `== -1`, or a type error) is a reconstruction defect. The trial found no hits
# either way, so this records intent rather than silencing evidence.
#
# Deliberately not gated, pending classification (see .clang-tidy-audit):
# - bugprone-suspicious-memory-comparison: 11 hits, all `memcmp` over
#   W8CombatSlot, whose 1-byte W8TargetKind at 0x00 leaves padding before
#   `int iChar` at 0x04 and so has no unique object representation. A raw block
#   compare is the plausible VC6 idiom and is what the retail machine code
#   would do; rewriting it member-wise would be a matching regression, not a
#   fix. This is evidence about the struct's layout, not a defect to repair.
# - bugprone-non-zero-enum-to-bool-conversion,
#   bugprone-implicit-widening-of-multiplication-result,
#   bugprone-tagged-union-member-count,
#   bugprone-undefined-memory-manipulation and
#   bugprone-string-literal-with-embedded-nul found zero hits tree-wide, so
#   they are cheap to keep reporting and expensive to trust blindly: an
#   incomplete recovered enum legitimately omits a sentinel value, and the
#   reconstruction uses large amounts of memset/memcpy that must not be
#   "fixed" to appease a heuristic. They stay in the non-gating audit profile.
Checks: >
  -*,
  wiz8-redundant-scalar-cast,
  wiz8-bool-like-byte,
  wiz8-project-record-reinterpret-cast,
  bugprone-misplaced-widening-cast,
  readability-redundant-casting,
  bugprone-sizeof-expression,
  bugprone-swapped-arguments,
  bugprone-suspicious-enum-usage,
  bugprone-pointer-arithmetic-on-polymorphic-object,
  readability-redundant-declaration,
  bugprone-chained-comparison,
  bugprone-infinite-loop,
  bugprone-misleading-setter-of-reference,
  bugprone-misplaced-operator-in-strlen-in-alloc,
  bugprone-misplaced-pointer-arithmetic-in-alloc,
  bugprone-suspicious-semicolon,
  bugprone-suspicious-string-compare
CheckOptions:
  bugprone-sizeof-expression.WarnOnSizeOfPointerToAggregate: 'false'
  bugprone-sizeof-expression.WarnOnSizeOfPointer: 'false'
  bugprone-suspicious-enum-usage.StrictMode: 'false'
  bugprone-pointer-arithmetic-on-polymorphic-object.IgnoreInheritedVirtualFunctions: 'true'
  bugprone-suspicious-string-compare.WarnOnImplicitComparison: 'false'
  bugprone-suspicious-string-compare.WarnOnLogicalNotComparison: 'false'
WarningsAsErrors: '*'
# Match first-party trees by repository-relative path so the same filter
# works under Docker's /repo mount, a local checkout, and relative
# compile-database entries. Do not hard-code /repo here.
HeaderFilterRegex: '(^|/)(include/wiz8|include/surrender|src/wiz8|src/surrender|src/srext_jpegimporter|src/srext_unzip)/'
FormatStyle: none
